WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
Shadow Minister for Health and Social  care laborers Liz Kendall joins me in  the studio lovely to see you this  morning nice to see you too  um I I wonder if I might just get a  little word from you on that situation  in solihull I mean I I cannot begin to  imagine what the parents of those poor  children are are going through but we  just need to remind our kids don't we  you know the ice might look thick the  ice might look safe but it may well not  be I think it is um every parent's  absolute worst nightmare  um I've just had a boy myself and first  thing I thought when I  saw this this morning was imagining how  I would feel and how important it is to  be careful and to warn children but  right now I just my heart goes out to  them and it has and to all their family  and friends you must be devastated too  they will be and congratulations to you  as well  um let's let's talk about the strikes  however and of course what we are seeing  today Unison members in Northern Ireland  will be going on strike in addition  we've also had that that official  request from the government to to bring  in the military to drive ambulances it's  all looking pretty Grim this winter when  it comes to the state of the Health  Service isn't it I mean it really is we  know already we've got seven million  patients on the waiting list four  hundred thousand waiting more than a  year it's not acceptable so that's why I  think that Steve Barkley the health  secretary should accept the offer from  the rcnn Unison this 11th Hour offer we  will pause the strikes they said if you  meet with us to discuss pay or if you  don't want to meet with us directly go  through the arbitration service acass I  personally think it's unforgivable that  he isn't meeting with them because  they've said we will pause the strikes  if you meet with us he needs to do that  and he needs to do that today if labor  were in government at the moment what  would they be offering nurses well we  have always wanted to see our nurses get  Fair pay when we were in government we  made sure that that's what happened but  I'm not going to promise you or your  viewers today pluck a figure out of  nowhere because God only knows what the  state if the economy is going to be in  two years time and we have only made  promises when we've showed how we'll pay  for them I think nurses deserve that but  we would absolutely meet discuss and  negotiate with them and we would always  show how we would pay for that sure but  but don't nurses also deserve to know  the general public does have to know  that whether or not labor would be  offering more money than is on the table  from the government of course we want to  see nurses have a fair pay rise  but I believe if you make a promise you  should be able to stick to it and that's  why we can't as I said pluck a figure  out of nowhere but let's just take a  step and criticize the government for  the way in which they are behaving  because they're not even meeting the  nurses that's what I'm criticizing them  for you know when we were in government  we regularly met uh doctors nurses to  discuss all of these issues I can't  believe they aren't just doing that but  let me just take a step back about why  we are in this situation in the first  place it is not just that the government  crashed the economy with their mini  budget their disastrous minutes but it's  that for 12 long years we've had no or  pathetically weak economic growth so we  haven't had the money to put into our  public services including for a fair pay  worth that is the reason we're in this  mess not simply because of the current  situation but because of this long  record that's what the government needs  to change okay but when it comes when it  comes to pain I'm sorry to keep laboring  this point when labor says it we  negotiate with with nursing unions you  seem to be implying that you had been in  essence be ripping up the independent  peer review body recommendations is that  correct no we we always use the  recommendations of the independent pay  review but negotiations have always  happened between employers and employees  you have to have those discussions  that's what the government has failed to  take action on I don't want to see those  strikes happening in the NHS if you you  know I used to run the ambulance service  network that represents all ambulance  trusts I know that paramedics those are  999 calls they don't go into this for  the money they go into it for a vocation  but my Hospital in Leicester has got a  food bank for nurses that's unacceptable  we need proper funding for our Public  Services by growing the economy and we  need a government that will actually sit  down and start those discussions why  that is the shadow Health secretary  picking a fight with the doctors unions  the nurses unions and so on and so forth  I mean a remarkable interview that he  gave to the Sunday Telegraph yesterday  you know this is labor the party of  Labor you know being openly critical  about these organizations saying that  they are vested interests and so on and  so forth I mean politically what on  Earth is he up to now actually if you  read the headline I don't if you read  the actual story not the headline it's  very different look Wes is absolutely  right to say we need more GPS that's why  Labor's plan will double the number of  medical school places uh funded by  getting rid of the non-dom tax status  but in return for that we also need to  see changes I don't want people waiting  for hours on the phone to get a GP  appointment people should be able to  have the right to see their doctor face  to face if they want that that's what  wiz was saying that is not the unions  had to be fair well that's what he said  I think it is not unreasonable for  people to be able to get to see their GP  and to be able to see them face to face  I'm sure that that's what your viewers  will think too so GPS are under  phenomenal pressure the that's why we  have spelled out how we will double the  number of medical school places  including for people who want to be GPS  but in return we've got to be able to  get you know my parents have struggled  uh they they live in Sussex ringing  ringing to try and see the GP and the GP  says unless it's an absolute emergency  we can't see that that's not right  that's not right but we need to change  the way things work just a word then on  on you know people working in the Health  Professions at the moment now you saw  what it was like on your way into the  studio this morning the Pavements will  ice up people will be falling in huge  numbers there will be people who require  care not necessarily urgent not  necessarily life in limb care but they  will require care that will not be able  to get it on these straight days because  of the stroke do you think that that  should serve not to focus the minds of  those in government but Focus minds of  those who are working on the front line  they really are focused you know if you  speak to anybody who's been working in  the NHS particular particularly during  covid they have given their all they've  risked their own lives by doing that  they are absolutely pushed to Breaking  Point here as I said having to my  hospital having to have a food bank  that's not right you know there are  already huge staff shortages and the  thing is this can be solved it can be  solved but the government needs to get  round the table and sort it out  congratulations again on the we won Buzz  Kendall thanks for being with us

